# TT.EVENT_INTERFACE -- newevent_new and addevent_new, the integration surface other schemas call.
# newevent_new: new-ticket branch for an automatic event (10004, subject composed from the first
# line of the details, S-EVENT-010/014), a customer e-mail (30002 -> ticket type 2, history event
# 101001, summary counters), the same with a Zitadel contact (ticket owner set without the admin
# check), a comment without host (company from the contact, S-EVENT-002), the inactive-host drop
# (S-EVENT-003), a host without mss.host2service row (S-EVENT-001 NO_DATA_FOUND arm: warning,
# company NULL), a host with TWO host2service rows (S-EVENT-001 TOO_MANY_ROWS re-raised, P0003),
# a nonexistent host (S-EVENT-003, P0002) and a nonexistent event type (S-EVENT-005, P0002), the
# append-to-recent-ticket path (S-EVENT-008/009: 10001 then 10003 on a host with an open automatic
# ticket -> addevent_new + change_status to hot), and details WITHOUT a newline for the two
# first-line extractions (SUBSTR(x, 1, INSTR(x, CHR(10)) - 1) with INSTR = 0).
# addevent_new: a public comment (rollups: last_public_event, summary/todo counters,
# fast_resolvable cleared, recoverable_status_id cleared, S-EVENT-030/031), a private comment, a
# notified comment (TT.OSAG_NOTIFY.event_notify with no listener configured), 30002 -> hot
# (S-EVENT-025), 10001 on a change ticket -> type 1 (S-EVENT-027), 30002 on an ISP-outage ticket
# -> type 1 (S-EVENT-026), 30016 -> fast_resolvable, the closed ticket (S-EVENT-021, OS980), the
# merged ticket (S-EVENT-019/020: recursion onto the merge target, org_ticket_id), a nonexistent
# ticket and a nonexistent event type (S-EVENT-016/017: swallowed by the outer handler).
#
# Ticket and event ids are sequence-generated and differ per engine: new tickets are selected by
# host/company and ordered by subject, their events by subject + type.
#
# What the first live run (2026-10-21) found, all resolved before this scenario went green:
#   * the fixture "host with TWO host2service rows" is impossible in Oracle -- unique index
#     MSS.IDX_H2S_HOST_UN (ORA-00001 in setup). Removed; spec S-EVENT-001 amended, pgTAP
#     re-pointed (TEST-AMENDMENTS A-026), schema-fixes/29 adds the index on PostgreSQL.
#   * single-line details: Oracle SUBSTR(x, 1, INSTR(x, CHR(10)) - 1) returns NULL, the
#     translation raised 22011 (and addevent_new's swallowing handler LOST the event) --
#     fixed in tt.event_interface (S-EVENT-048, firstline suite).
#   * the 101003 status-change event written through ticket_interface.change_status had
#     details_public NULL on PostgreSQL (NULL concatenation of the NULL p_details_public) --
#     fixed in tt.ticket_interface (S-TICKET-064, nullconcat suite).
# Note also that the 10004 events of steps 01/13 are APPENDED to the open automatic ticket
# 957102 (same host, first event 10001 of source 1, ticket type 1 -- S-EVENT-008's "others are
# appended to automatically generated trouble tickets" arm) on both engines, not opened as new
# tickets; step 13's event is the one the pre-fix translation lost.
#
# ORA_USER=system: the fixtures insert into stop.company, stop.contact, mss.host, mss.service and
# mss.host2service; TT holds only SELECT on those. Rolled back at the end (COMMITS=no); on Oracle
# only the autonomous plog rows survive.
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=newevent_new (new ticket, drop, append, S-EVENT-001/002/003/005 error paths, first-line subject without newline) and addevent_new (rollups, hot, type changes, closed, merged, swallowed errors)
